      "claim": "L1 human absolute/relative oral bioavailability records for structurally related fused pyrimidine, pyridylmethyl, and polar heteroaromatic molecules are predominantly at or above 20%: piritrexim 23-75% (C08, C09, C10, C15), vatalanib 58% (C03), nilotinib 31% fasted (C04), naratriptan 63-74% (C02, C05, C12, C19), isoniazid 78-93% (C14, C16), bromfenac 67% (C06, C11, C13, C18), and CP-409,092 human 69% (C01).",
