      "claim": "Low L2 F values are species-mismatched and do not affirm a low human F for the query: IQG-607 in mice ~4% (C25, C30) and CP-409,092 in rats <3% (C28, C31), whereas human CP-409,092 RBA is 69% (C01).",
      "card_ids": ["C25","C28","C30","C31"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 absorption/solubility records for related polar heterocycles support adequate absorption/dissolution: theophylline almost completely absorbed (C56, C57), trimethoprim well absorbed (C48, C51), and related pyrimidinone/guanine-like solubilities of 0.8-2.5 mg/mL (C50, C54, C58, C59).",
      "card_ids": ["C48","C49","C50","C51","C54","C56","C57","C58","C59"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 gut-wall records show high permeability and no efflux liability for related molecules: isoniazid Papp 16.4-22.7 x10^-6 cm/s with efflux ratios 1.18-1.19 (C62-C65, C70, C71), pyridopyrimidinediones are not P-gp substrates (C66, C68, C69), imatinib ileal efflux ratio is 1.0 (C61), and carbovir absorption is uniform across intestinal segments (C67).",
      "card_ids": ["C61","C62","C63","C64","C65","C66","C67","C68","C69","C70","C71"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic-clearance records show low-to-moderate intrinsic clearance for related pyridine/pyrimidinone/guanine-like molecules: pyridine analogues CLint <15 (C72), compound 16 CLint <14 (C79), thiolactone 2 CLint 8.03 (C80), O6-benzylguanine Clint 2.3-18 and predicted hepatic clearance 11.2 ml/min/kg (C73, C74, C77, C81), vonoprazan CLint 2.73 (C75), and rat hepatocyte CLint 3.9 (C76). No L6 record shows high first-pass clearance.",
      "card_ids": ["C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C79","C80","C81"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C79","C80","C81"]
